From f27f163bc6cbf60a9ce6971494f5ae4d441db00a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roberto <RobertoD91@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:13:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add USB HID FIDO mode for CTAPHID authenticators

Adds USB_HID_DEVICE_MODE_FIDO to the USB HID device driver: the FIDO
Alliance report map (usage page 0xF1D0) with 64-byte IN and OUT reports
and an interrupt OUT endpoint, send_raw() to send IN reports and
set_raw_report_callback() to receive OUT reports. An app can present the
device to a host as a FIDO2/U2F security key over CTAPHID.

Enables the usbdevicehid0 child on the ESP32-S3 devices that already
have a usbdevice0 node, so the HID class driver is built for them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UAYrYnr6tvN7SQKimwgNxa
